#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the IBM Cloud Resource Controller REST API to get, list, update, and create IBM Quantum Compute Service instances."
msgstr "Verwende die IBM Cloud Resource Controller REST API, um IBM Quantum Compute Service-Instanzen abzurufen, aufzulisten, zu aktualisieren und zu erstellen."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Cloud Resource Controller API for instance management"
msgstr "IBM Cloud Resource Controller API für die Instanzverwaltung verwenden"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "{/* cspell:ignore ResourceController  */}\n"
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Abluemix, apikey */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore ResourceController  */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Cloud Resource Controller API for instance management {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"
msgstr "IBM Cloud Resource Controller API für die Instanzverwaltung verwenden {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use the IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller REST API to programmatically get, create, and update [instances](/guides/instances). \n"
msgstr "Du kannst die IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller REST API verwenden, um [Instanzen](/guides/instances) programmgesteuert abzurufen, zu erstellen und zu aktualisieren. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All Resource Controller endpoints require that you authenticate by passing a header called `Authorization` with the bearer token. Refer to the [REST API setup guide](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"
msgstr "Für alle Resource Controller-Endpunkte ist eine Authentifizierung erforderlich. Übergib dazu einen Header namens `Authorization` mit dem Bearer-Token. Weitere Informationen findest du im [Leitfaden zur Einrichtung der REST-API](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get an instance {#get-an-instance}"
msgstr "Eine Instanz abrufen {#get-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance) endpoint to get information about a particular instance. The [CRN](/guides/instances) must be URL-encoded in the path.\n"
msgstr "Verwende den Endpunkt [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance), um Informationen zu einer bestimmten Instanz abzurufen. Die [CRN](/guides/instances) muss im Pfad URL-codiert sein.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the standard Resource Controller fields, the response includes quantum-specific fields in both `parameters` and `extensions`. `extensions` stores the instance's normalized metadata, whereas `parameters` only stores the most recent request to modify the instance. Therefore, you should read from `extensions` rather than `parameters`.\n"
msgstr "Zusätzlich zu den Standardfeldern des Resource Controllers enthält die Antwort quantenspezifische Felder sowohl in `parameters` als auch in `extensions`. `extensions` speichert die normalisierten Metadaten der Instanz, während `parameters` nur die letzte Anfrage zur Änderung der Instanz speichert. Daher solltest du aus `extensions` und nicht aus `parameters` lesen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `extensions` object includes these fields:\n"
msgstr "Das Objekt `extensions` enthält die folgenden Felder:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`instance_limit_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The usage time limit for the instance. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`instance_limit_seconds` — Integer oder `null`. Das Nutzungszeitlimit für die Instanz. Siehe [Zuteilungslimits für Instanzen festlegen](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The time allocated to this instance, used by the [fair-share scheduler](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) to determine queue priority. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Integer oder `null`. Die dieser Instanz zugewiesene Zeit, die vom [Fair-Share-Scheduler](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) genutzt wird, um die Priorität in der Warteschlange zu bestimmen. Siehe [Zuteilungslimits für Instanzen festlegen](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`backends` — Array of strings. The allowlist of backend names available to this instance. `[\"ANY\"]` means all backends on the plan are available (the default). `[]` means no backends are available.\n"
msgstr "`backends` — Array von Strings. Die Erlaubnisliste der Backend-Namen, die für diese Instanz verfügbar sind. `[\"ANY\"]` bedeutet, dass alle Backends des Plans verfügbar sind (Standard). `[]` bedeutet, dass keine Backends verfügbar sind.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"The backends field may be outdated\">\n"
"  The `backends` field in the `extensions` object may be outdated. This can happen when IBM Quantum Support changes your account in a way that impacts instances. For example, when a backend is removed from an account, it will update the `backends` for the instance, but that change is currently not yet reflected in the Resource Controller API.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Das Feld „backends“ ist möglicherweise veraltet\">\n"
"  Das Feld `backends` im Objekt `extensions` ist möglicherweise veraltet. Dies kann passieren, wenn der IBM Quantum-Support dein Konto so ändert, dass sich dies auf Instanzen auswirkt. Wenn beispielsweise ein Backend aus einem Konto entfernt wird, werden die `backends` für die Instanz aktualisiert, diese Änderung wird jedoch derzeit noch nicht in der Resource Controller API berücksichtigt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Instead, the current workaround is to use the [IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) with the [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends) endpoint. (Make sure that you set the `Service-CRN` header to your instance's CRN.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Der aktuelle Workaround besteht stattdessen darin, die [IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) mit dem Endpunkt [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends) zu verwenden. (Stelle sicher, dass du den Header `Service-CRN` auf die CRN deiner Instanz setzt.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    The CRN must be URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    Die CRN muss im Pfad URL-codiert sein. Ersetze jeden `:` durch `%3A` und jeden `/` durch `%2F`. Zum Beispiel wird `crn:v1:bluemix:...` zu `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request GET \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request GET \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import urllib.parse\n"
"    import requests\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import urllib.parse\n"
"    import requests\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # We use urllib.parse.quote to URL-encode the CRN.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # We use urllib.parse.quote to URL-encode the CRN.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
